  "reviewed_interpretation": "The single authoritative I034 execution is valid and terminal. All preregistered coverage gates passed, all four fixed post-target reference horizons had full coverage among 52 causal-anchor cases, and shipping NS/VAD mirrors remained exact. Across horizons 1/2/4/8, median absolute shipping-NS response remained only 1.16-1.36 dB while the post-NS local observation response remained 5.93-7.40 dB. The global median absolute NS/local response ratio stayed approximately 0.18-0.20 rather than increasing with horizon. Median absolute alignment error moved 6.96 -> 6.67 -> 5.32 -> 6.90 dB and p90 error 12.05 -> 13.93 -> 15.50 -> 14.21 dB, so there is no monotonic fixed-horizon catch-up. H4 is descriptive only and cannot be promoted as a selected lag or horizon. I034 therefore does not support a lag-only explanation for I033; it supports a persistent response-amplitude/domain mismatch that still requires mechanism decomposition. No lag, tracker alpha, refresh rule, mapping, threshold or source candidate is selected.",
