  "proposed_followup_hypothesis": {
    "id": "i035-ns-noise-tracker-update-regime-decomposition-v1",
    "authority": "CANDIDATE_ZERO_DIAGNOSTIC_ONLY",
    "rationale": "Use fresh public-development target seeds and unchanged shipping NS/VAD source. Preserve the I034 causal target/anchor and fixed 1/2/4/8 post-target reference horizons. Extend diagnostic-only mirror observation to decompose the existing EMA noise tracker update regime: fixed slow-update branch exposure (speech_probability > 0.35), fast-update exposure, post-ratio pressure, and aggregate slow/fast-bin contribution to noise-estimate movement at the target and fixed horizons. Test whether the persistent NS response deficit co-varies with slow-update exposure or remains after update opportunity is available. Do not change or search alpha, select a horizon/lag, normalize scale, choose a refresh rule, threshold or source candidate.",
